Real environment tested: macOS (Darwin), real production modules from this branch run with tsx: `writeLaunchAgentPlist` (the install writer) and `rewriteLaunchAgentPlistForRestart` (the restart rewrite step), plus `readLaunchAgentProgramArguments` (service readCommand). The run used real `/usr/bin/plutil`, the real filesystem under a throwaway HOME/OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR with an isolated profile label, and real `/bin/sh` sourcing of the resulting env file. Nothing was stubbed. The same driver ran on pristine main fd69a4eedd and on the patched tree. No live Gateway was restarted.
