## What Problem This Solves

Fixes external CLI credentials being reported as absent when their JSON file points through more than one symbolic link, even though the same path can be written successfully.

## User Impact

Managed credential files such as `.gemini/oauth_creds.json -> active.json -> payload.json` can be discovered through the existing reader. Regular files and one-link paths retain their behavior. Missing, cyclic, invalid and unreadable targets remain absent; links are not replaced.

## Why This Change Was Made

The explicit through-symlink reader resolved one hop, then handed a remaining symbolic link to the regular-file-only JSON reader. Resolve the target chain before that same no-follow reader opens the final file. The existing write owner already resolves complete chains; it is unchanged.

This adds no configuration, protocol, schema, migration, dependency, or permission surface. Existing input-path errors and tolerant target-read behavior are preserved. Production: **+8/-1 (net +7)** for full-chain resolution and its read-error boundary; tests: **+49/-0**. Two files changed. AI-assisted implementation, source review and verification.

